---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Cta from '../components/home/Cta.astro';

const rows: [string, string][] = [
  ['Session', 'Task. Starting it creates the worktree and opens a terminal in it.'],
  ['n, N (new session, with a prompt)', 'New task. The prompt goes on the card, and the start hook hands it to the agent. ⌘N opens the composer from anywhere.'],
  ['default_program and profiles', 'Start hook, per project, such as claude "$OUIJIT_TASK_DESCRIPTION".'],
  ['cs -p codex', 'A different start hook, or a one-off command when you start the task.'],
  ['-y, --autoyes', 'Run the agent with its permission checks off, in a sandbox that holds it to the worktree.'],
  ['tmux session; ↵ to attach, ctrl-q to detach', 'A terminal card. Click it. Nothing to attach or detach, and no tmux.'],
  ['Preview tab', "The terminal itself, live. Each card shows whether its agent is thinking or waiting."],
  ['Diff tab', 'Diff review, with notes the agent reads'],
  ['s (commit and push)', 'From the terminal, or a done hook that pushes. Pull requests from the project menu.'],
  ['c (checkout), r (resume)', 'Quit and relaunch. Quitting saves the session, and the next launch restores the terminals in their worktrees.'],
  ['D (kill session)', 'Trash the task. The worktree goes to the system trash.'],
  ['↑/↓, j/k', 'The sidebar, or ⌘K to jump to any terminal, task or project.'],
  ['One branch per session', 'One branch and worktree per task, named after the task number, such as T-42.'],
  ['tmux and gh', 'Nothing. gh only for the pull request surface.'],
];
---
<Site
  title="Claude Squad alternative · Ouijit"
  description="Moving from Claude Squad to Ouijit: how sessions, profiles, auto-yes and the preview and diff tabs map onto tasks, hooks, the sandbox and diff review.">
  <main class="compare-content">
    <h1>Coming from Claude Squad</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      If you used Claude Squad, you already know how Ouijit works. Each task gets a git worktree and an agent, and
      the agent is still a CLI in a terminal. Here's how the pieces line up.
    </p>
    <img
      class="compare-screenshot"
      src="/assets/screenshots/kanban.png"
      alt="A project's board with tasks in To Do, In Progress, In Review and Done, and their terminals in the sidebar"
      loading="lazy"
    />

    <h2>Why Ouijit</h2>
    <p>
      The agents run as their own CLIs in real terminals, in their worktrees, with no tmux in between. The board
      shows what each one is doing without attaching to it, and a sound or notification tells you when a turn ends.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every agent gets the <a href="/docs/cli/"><code>ouijit</code> command</a>. Ask it to split a feature into
      tasks and it starts them, each with its own agent. It can read the other agents' terminals, open its plan
      beside itself, link you to the line it changed, and stage review comments for you to send.
    </p>
    <p>
      Auto-yes becomes safe. A task can run in a <a href="/docs/sandbox/">sandbox</a>, so an agent with permission
      checks off is held to its worktree. Ouijit is free, open source, and runs on macOS and Linux.
    </p>

    <h2>What maps to what</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Claude Squad</th><th>Ouijit</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map(([a, b]) => (
          <tr><td>{a}</td><td>{b}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>What you give up</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Living in one terminal. Ouijit is a desktop app, and the terminals live in it.</li>
      <li>Gemini, Aider and Amp integration. Any CLI runs in an Ouijit terminal, but only Claude Code, Codex, Pi and OpenCode get live status and the <code>ouijit</code> command.</li>
      <li>A daemon that presses Enter for the agent. Run the agent with its permission checks off instead, in the sandbox.</li>
      <li>One key to commit and push. Do it from the terminal, or put it in a done hook.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Move a project over</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Push or finish your Claude Squad sessions. Ouijit makes its own worktrees.</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/">Install Ouijit</a> and open the repository as a project.</li>
      <li>Under <strong>Project Settings → Hooks</strong>, put your <code>default_program</code> command in the start hook with the task's prompt, for example <code>claude "$OUIJIT_TASK_DESCRIPTION"</code>.</li>
      <li>If you ran with <code>--autoyes</code>, add <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> to that command and set the hook to run in the sandbox.</li>
      <li>For pull requests in the app, enable them under <strong>Project Settings → Experimental</strong> and run <code>gh auth login</code>.</li>
    </ol>
  </main>
  <Cta />
</Site>
